---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectTrail from '../../components/ProjectTrail.astro';
import { stitcher } from '../../data/metrics';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
import '../../styles/project.css';
import s20 from '../../assets/stitcher/stages/stage-20.webp';
import s40 from '../../assets/stitcher/stages/stage-40.webp';
import s60 from '../../assets/stitcher/stages/stage-60.webp';
import s80 from '../../assets/stitcher/stages/stage-80.webp';
import s91 from '../../assets/stitcher/stages/stage-91.webp';

const p = projects.find((x) => x.slug === 'image-stitcher')!;
const stages = [[20, s20], [40, s40], [60, s60], [80, s80], [91, s91]] as const;
---
<Base
  title="Image Stitcher: one map from several drones | Abtin Aryanpour"
  description="A groundside stitcher for the Waterloo Aerial Robotics Group that merges out-of-order, GPS-tagged photos from several drones into one georeferenced map. Tested in simulation; the pull request is in review."
  current="work"
>
  <article class="proj">
    <header class="top">
      <div class="top-sky"><ProjectTrail start={p.start} end={p.end} /></div>
      <div class="top-text wrap">
        <h1 class="display">Image Stitcher</h1>
        <p class="lead">Merges out-of-order, GPS-tagged photos from several drones into one top-down map that sits in the right place on the Earth.</p>
        <p class="status">In review. Built on the autonomy software team at the Waterloo Aerial Robotics Group, from October 2026. The pull request is open, with changes requested. <a href="https://github.com/UWARG/autonomy-monorepo/pull/215">Pull request #215 on GitHub</a></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="stages-sec wrap" aria-label="The map as it grows">
      <figure class="stages">
        <ol>
          {stages.map(([n, img]) => (
            <li>
              <Picture src={img} fallbackFormat="webp" formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[400, 700, 1100]} sizes="(max-width: 759px) 46vw, 19vw" alt={`The map after ${n} photos`} />
              <span class="small num">{n} photos</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
        <figcaption class="small">One simulated mission, saved after 20, 40, 60, 80 and all 91 photos, each drawn in the same GPS frame. The stepped outline is the edge of the stitched photos, and only the painted ground markers are kept inside it.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="why wrap" aria-labelledby="why-h">
      <h2 id="why-h" class="visually-hidden">Why it exists</h2>
      <p class="statement">Drones fly back and forth over a field taking photos. The photos reach the ground laptop out of order, from several drones, with GPS that’s metres off and no compass heading.</p>
      <p class="why-more">GPS finds which photos should overlap, image matching lines them up, and all the GPS readings together place the finished map on the Earth.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="results wrap grid" aria-labelledby="results-h">
      <h2 id="results-h">One connected map in {stitcher.missions} simulated missions</h2>
      <div class="chart">
        <table class="facts-table">
          <caption class="small">All simulated: 10 missions of 91 photos from 3 drones, arriving shuffled, with the heading unknown.</caption>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">One connected map</th><td>{stitcher.missions} missions, at 1 m and 3 m of GPS error</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Photo-to-photo alignment</th><td><span class="num">{stitcher.alignment}</span>, at most about 1.5 pixels</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Least-squares refinement</th><td>Misalignment of <span class="num">{stitcher.refineBefore}</span> without it, <span class="num">{stitcher.refineAfter}</span> with it</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Map position against the truth</th><td><span class="num">{stitcher.mapError}</span></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Speed</th><td><span class="num">{stitcher.speed}</span> per photo on a laptop CPU</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Tests</th><td>{stitcher.tests} stitcher tests, plus a ground-truth mission simulator</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="notes">
        <p>The simulator knows where every photo really was, so each run can be scored against the truth instead of by eye.</p>
        <p>Alignment is how far apart the same ground point lands in two neighbouring photos. Map position is how far the whole map sits from where it should be on the Earth.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="how wrap grid" aria-labelledby="how-h">
      <h2 id="how-h">From shuffled photos to one map</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><p><b>Check.</b> Each photo is undistorted for the lens, then checked for blur, exposure and tilt before it’s used.</p></li>
        <li><p><b>Find neighbours.</b> GPS says which photos should overlap, even when they arrive out of order from different drones.</p></li>
        <li><p><b>Match.</b> XFeat learned features and RANSAC line each pair up and throw out wrong matches.</p></li>
        <li><p><b>Recover heading.</b> There’s no compass, so the matches and the noisy GPS together work out which way each photo faces.</p></li>
        <li><p><b>Refine.</b> A least-squares solver, in the style of bundle adjustment, adjusts every photo at once so the whole map agrees.</p></li>
        <li><p><b>Place.</b> All the GPS readings together put the finished map in the right place on the Earth.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="story wrap" aria-labelledby="hard-h">
      <h2 id="hard-h" class="visually-hidden">What was hard</h2>
      <div class="problem">
        <h3>Rows wouldn’t connect</h3>
        <p>The drones turn 180 degrees at the end of each row, and XFeat isn’t rotation invariant. In simulated missions, of 600 candidate matches between rows, only {stitcher.rowMatches.replace(' of 600', '')} survived RANSAC. Extracting features at four quarter turns fixed it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem">
        <h3>Refinement made the map worse</h3>
        <p>The first version gave simulated errors of 20 to 30 m, because a huge penalty weight on the pinned photo made the solver unstable. Removing that photo’s unknowns from the system fixed it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem">
        <h3>One simulated run in 10 split the map</h3>
        <p>Small clusters with noisy GPS rejected good matches. Now a cluster’s GPS check only counts once the cluster spans four times the GPS error, and a repeating-ground test proves wrong matches stay blocked.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem">
        <h3>The blur check rejected good photos</h3>
        <p>Sharp and blurred scores overlapped, so no limit could work. The new score compares a photo with itself at half resolution, in each direction. Code review then showed sensor noise could fool it, so a 3×3 median filter runs first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem">
        <h3>Where it still falls short</h3>
        <p>Every result is from simulation. There are no real flight photos yet. It assumes flat ground and a camera pointing straight down, the blur limits are tuned on synthetic photos, and it isn’t connected to live drone comms. The pull request hasn’t merged.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="next wrap grid" aria-labelledby="next-h">
      <h2 id="next-h">Where it stands</h2>
      <div class="next-text">
        <p>The stitcher is a pull request to the team’s autonomy code, reviewed by the autonomy subteam. The second round of review changes was pushed on November 3, 2026.</p>
        <p class="small dim">Built with Python, PyTorch, OpenCV, NumPy and pytest.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="onward wrap" aria-label="Next project">
      <a class="display" href="/projects/doppel/">Next project: Doppel.exe</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .stages-sec { padding-top: var(--s8); }
  .stages { margin: 0; }
  .stages ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--gap); }
  .stages li { display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }
  .stages li span { color: var(--dim); }
  .stages :global(img) { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .stages figcaption { margin-top: var(--s4); color: var(--dim); max-width: 64ch; }
  @media (max-width: 759px) {
    .stages ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .stages li:last-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  }
</style>
